menu "WATCHA BSP"

    config WATCHA_BATTERY_PROFILE_WANLI_500MAH
        bool "Use the Wanli New Energy 500 mAh CW2017 profile"
        default n
        help
            Selects which of the two vendor CW2017 profiles the BSP writes into the
            fuel gauge. The two profiles describe different cells: 51 of the 80 bytes
            differ, so the state-of-charge curve changes completely.

            Default (n): the UTL 520 mAh profile carried by the upstream
            WatchaAI/WATCHA-POCKET firmware and by this fork up to v0.1.3.

            y: the Wanli New Energy 500 mAh profile2 / XIL40X dated 2026-10-20,
            ported from ai-passport.

            This choice only changes the 80 profile bytes. It does not alter the
            charging circuit, charge current, voltage limits, pin map, Flash
            partitions, or the NVS layout. Replacing the cell requires a profile
            generated for that cell plus renewed charge/discharge validation.

endmenu
